Vercel Web Analytics Installation Complete
==========================================

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

Changes Made:
-------------

1. **Installed @vercel/analytics package**
   - Added @vercel/analytics dependency to package.json
   - Updated package-lock.json with new dependency

2. **Modified app/layout.tsx**
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
   - Inserted `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body section
   - Component placement follows official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router

Implementation Details:
-----------------------

- Framework: Next.js 16.2.3 (App Router)
- Package Manager: npm
- Documentation Source: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Analytics Package Version: Latest from npm registry

The Analytics component has been placed in the root layout file (app/layout.tsx) to ensure it tracks all routes across the application. The component is rendered at the end of the body tag, following Vercel's official Next.js App Router implementation guidelines.

Next Steps:
-----------

To enable analytics tracking in production:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel project dashboard under the Analytics tab
3. Once deployed, analytics will automatically begin tracking page views and web vitals

Verification:
